    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.clustering_coefficient - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.clustering_coefficient.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.clustering_coefficient()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate local clustering coefficient for each node.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.clustering_coefficient()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate local clustering coefficient for each node.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.clustering_coefficient()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Calculate local clustering coefficient for each node.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCalculate local clustering coefficient for each node.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L38073-L38210){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.clustering_coefficient(\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Clustering coefficient](../assets/graphs/clustering-coefficient.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The shared seven-node graph shaded by each node's clustering coefficient. A's two neighbors are linked, so A scores 1.00, then B and D 0.67, C 0.50 and E 0.33. Nodes with fewer than two neighbors get 0 rather than None, so the pendant G ties with F at 0.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe clustering coefficient measures the degree to which a node's neighbors are connected to\neach other. For a node `v`:\n\n`C(v) = (number of edges between neighbors) / (number of possible edges between neighbors)\n     = (2 × triangles through v) / (degree(v) × (degree(v) - 1))`\n\nOn a directed graph this is Fagiolo's directed clustering, which counts every directed\ntriangle through `v` whatever the directions of its arcs (see\n`local_clustering_coefficient()` for the formula); it matches `networkx.clustering()`.\nParallel edges and self-loops are ignored.\n\nReturns `0.0` for nodes with degree < `2` (cannot form triangles).\n\nRange: `[0, 1]` where:\n\n- `0` = neighbors are not connected at all\n- `1` = neighbors form a complete graph (clique)\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute to store clustering coefficient values. If `None`, uses\n    `clustering_coefficient` as the attribute name.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary mapping node IDs to clustering coefficients. If `False`,\n    stores values as node attributes and returns the Graph for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[int, float] or Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to clustering coefficients\n    (`0.0` to `1.0`). If `return_dict=` is `False`: returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe local clustering coefficient\n$C(v) = \\dfrac{2\\,\\Delta(v)}{k(v)(k(v) - 1)}$ (with $\\Delta(v)$ the number of triangles\\\ncontaining $v$ and $k(v)$ its degree) counts the fraction of possible edges among $v$'s\nneighbors that actually exist. Values near $1$ mean the neighborhood is essentially a\nclique. Values near $0$ mean it is tree-like. Averaging $C(v)$ across the graph produces the\nnetwork-level statistic Watts and Strogatz (1998) used to identify small-world structure:\nhigh local clustering combined with short average path lengths.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~local_clustering_coefficient`) \n\n:   The same values, with None for low degree.\n\n[](`~average_clustering_coefficient`) \n\n:   The mean over all nodes.\n\n[](`~square_clustering`) \n\n:   Clustering by squares instead of triangles.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nIn a triangle with a tail, `A` and `B` score 1, as their two neighbors are linked. `C`\nhas three neighbors and one linked pair among them, for 1/3. `D` has only one neighbor,\nand scores 0:\n\n::: {#d9ac6def .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"A\"), (\"C\", \"D\")]\n)\ngraph.clustering_coefficient()\n\ngraph.get_node_df().select(\"label\", \"clustering_coefficient\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (4, 2)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>clustering_coefficient</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;A&quot;</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;B&quot;</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;C&quot;</td><td>0.333333</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;D&quot;</td><td>0.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n`local_clustering_coefficient()` computes the same values, but leaves `D` undefined:\n\n::: {#371935da .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nd = graph.get_id_from_label(\"D\")\n(\n    graph.clustering_coefficient(return_dict=True)[d],\n    graph.local_clustering_coefficient(return_dict=True)[d],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(0.0, None)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Tight circles\n\n`friends()` links 24 members of two clubs in a made-up town, a chess club and a climbing\nclub, who are friends. Uma's two friends, Wes and Zane, are friends too, so Uma scores 1.\nNone of Rosa's three friends know each other, so Rosa scores 0:\n\n::: {#c3bef2c4 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends = ec.friends().clustering_coefficient()\n\n(\n    friends.get_node_df()\n    .sort(\"clustering_coefficient\", descending=True)\n    .select(\"label\", \"club\", \"degree\", \"clustering_coefficient\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (24, 4)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>club</th><th>degree</th><th>clustering_coefficient</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>str</td><td>i64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;Uma&quot;</td><td>&quot;Climbing&quot;</td><td>2</td><td>1.0</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Cleo&quot;</td><td>&quot;Chess&quot;</td><td>3</td><td>0.666667</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Iris&quot;</td><td>&quot;Chess&quot;</td><td>3</td><td>0.666667</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Kemal&quot;</td><td>&quot;Chess&quot;</td><td>4</td><td>0.666667</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Lou&quot;</td><td>&quot;Chess&quot;</td><td>3</td><td>0.666667</td></tr><tr><td>&hellip;</td><td>&hellip;</td><td>&hellip;</td><td>&hellip;</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Zane&quot;</td><td>&quot;Climbing&quot;</td><td>4</td><td>0.333333</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Ben&quot;</td><td>&quot;Chess&quot;</td><td>5</td><td>0.3</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Jules&quot;</td><td>&quot;Chess&quot;</td><td>5</td><td>0.3</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Oona&quot;</td><td>&quot;Climbing&quot;</td><td>5</td><td>0.3</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;Rosa&quot;</td><td>&quot;Climbing&quot;</td><td>3</td><td>0.0</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nHugo and Tara, a couple who link the two clubs, score only 0.4. Their friends come from\nboth clubs and don't know each other, so every triangle through one of them includes the\nother:\n\n::: {#6e64946a .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfriends.plot(color_by=\"clustering_coefficient\", label_by=\"label\", seed=8)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-48513e49:#345e95;--ect-d77ae92f:#5d8ac2;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-6826a5f9:#608ec6;--ect-9d43aea2:#5480b8;--ect-f8094ac6:#79a8e1;--ect-472663e1:#6d9bd3;--ect-5ee57d66:#4874ab;--ect-3c980f0e:#3c679e;--ect-ec386ef0:#305a91;--ect-97f76ec5:#254e84;--ect-e28c6970:#194278;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-cc7dc6b1:#244168;--ect-9c85670b:#416087;--ect-6970a796:#5d7fa7;--ect-bf50105f:#09254a;--ect-6649ad86:#43638a;--ect-98b1bca7:#3a5980;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ec